          "alt": "Source question figure."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "The figure shown is a right circular cylinder with a radius of *r* and height of *h*. A second right circular cylinder (not shown) has a volume that is 392 times as large as the volume of the cylinder shown. Which of the following could represent the radius *R*, in terms of *r*, and the height *H*, in terms of *h*, of the second cylinder?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "gengdu-export",
        "sourceSetId": "gengdu-offline-e676d12d27ea408894de749c8c13ee77",
        "sourceQuestionId": "8900498",
        "url": "https://gengdu.shanmaostar.com"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "*R* = 8*r* and *H* = 7*h*"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "*R* = 8*r* and *H* = 49*h*"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "*R* = 7*r* and *H* = 8*h*"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "*R* = 49*r* and *H* = 8*h*"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
